# render_state_depth: Depth and stencil, drawn over a memoryless depth-stencil attachment cleared to depth 1 and stencil 3: 0x68 SetDepthStencilState (compare Less keeps the nearer red over a farther green; Always lets green win; a stencil compare Equal passes with 0x77 reference 3 and fails with 4), 0x6c SetDepthBias pushing an equal-depth draw behind, 0x6d SetDepthClipMode clip or clamp for a triangle at z 1.5; 0x69, 0x6a (decoded as SetDepthStoreAction too), 0x78 and 0x79 on the memoryless attachment; 0x94 and 0x95 SetDepthCleared and SetStencilCleared. A private depth-stencil attachment keeps its load and store actions (only a memoryless one has them rewritten): a pass that stores depth 0.5 and a pass that loads it, where a farther green fails Less.
